  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID ClimAct Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  USAID&apos;s ClimAct Activity will strengthen the policy environment and governance structure, making it favorable for transformational changes in key systems aiming at net-zero emissions and a climate-resilient Bangladesh. This activity aims to catalyze long-term systemic shifts in Bangladesh&apos;s economy, institutions, and governance structures through interventions such as enabling policy development, facilitating technology transfer, bolstering climate research, and catalyzing the scaling of climate actions. With FY 2024 funds, the activity will develop local-level adaptation actions in selected climate hot spots, enhance local government institutions&apos; capacity for climate planning and monitoring, and establish an information portal to track adaptation and mitigation objectives. The activity will provide technical assistance to the government in issuing resilience bonds, conducting feasibility studies to establish the maiden carbon market, and collaborating with private sector insurers to develop and improve index insurance for natural disasters. The private sector finance mobilized under this activity would be utilized for climate-resilience agriculture energy-efficient practices.   The activity aligns with the priorities of the Government of Bangladesh in achieving its mitigation and adaptation targets. By strengthening Bangladesh&apos;s transformative capacity, the activity contributes to the U.S. Embassy&apos;s goal of making Bangladesh a socially and environmentally resilient country. Funding for the activity contributes to Adaptation-Indirect (300k), Global Food Security (500k), Private Sector Engagement ($150k) directives and key issues.</narrative>
  </description>
